# Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.x · .NET 10 · Class marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4** (of 7)   |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test  
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Integration calibration:** NOT downgraded — `Thread.Sleep` introduces non-determinism and slows the suite regardless of test scope.

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← arbitrary 3-second wait
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with timeout:**
```csharp
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
{
    if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
        return; // pass
    await Task.Delay(50);
}
Assert.Fail("Notification was not sent within timeout.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow CI agents; unnecessary 3 s added to every run.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic  
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch executes per run — the other path is never verified. If the production code flips types, the weaker branch silently passes.

**Fix — separate tests per type or assert deterministically:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — one code path is never validated.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Empty Test  
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← no assertion; passes even if inserts silently fail
```

**Note:** The name implies "no-exception = pass" intent, but this gives false confidence — a silently corrupted insert still passes.

**Fix — assert the outcome:**
```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage shows green while bugs hide.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (extended catalog)  
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, zero message parameters
```

**Problem:** When one fails in CI, the error reads `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no context about *which property* was wrong until you open the source.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be found after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should match inserted value");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should match inserted value");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis, especially in CI logs.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining 3 tests are well-designed:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear Arrange-Act-Assert, single concern, explicit assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Minimal setup, single assertion on absence |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Clean async coordination via `Task.WhenAll`, no sleep, verified outcome |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Self-documenting count (3 items added → assert 3), uses `CollectionAssert` |

The use of in-memory SQLite also deserves praise — it avoids the **Mystery Guest** smell by keeping the database hermetic and self-contained.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message params to assertions | ~3 min |

Fix items 1–3 first — they all risk **false-pass** (tests that succeed while bugs exist). Item 4 is a maintainability improvement for diagnosis speed.
